<p><strong>Bridal makeup studios in Nepal should book each artist by date and time so one artist is never promised to two weddings, record the advance against every booking, track trial and wedding-day sessions as a package, and see what is still owed. Zennly supports this for bridal and makeup studios.</strong></p>
<p>Wedding dates in Nepal cluster around auspicious days, so a studio can have many brides wanting the same morning. The cost of a mistake is enormous: a double-booked artist is a ruined wedding and a lost reputation. This is the clearest case for replacing the phone and the notebook with a system that locks the slot.</p>
<h2>Four things a bridal studio must control</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The artist's date and time.</strong> Once booked, it stays booked. See <a href="/features/booking/">booking management</a>.</li>
<li><strong>The advance.</strong> Record what the bride paid and what is still due on the booking.</li>
<li><strong>The package.</strong> Trial session, wedding day, and extras for family are one bundle. See <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Travel and location.</strong> Note outside-studio bookings so the artist is not also booked in the studio.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Wedding season is a rush, not a normal week</h2>
<p>Dashain-to-Tihar and the wedding months are when many Nepal studios earn most of their year. Set up artists, services, packages and prices before the peak, and let brides book online so the phone is free for exceptions. Learn more about <a href="/solutions/bridal-makeup/">booking software for bridal and makeup studios</a>.</p>
<h2>Related studio types</h2>
<p>Many parlours offer bridal work too. See <a href="/blog/beauty-parlour-software-nepal/">beauty parlour software</a> and <a href="/solutions/beauty-clinic/">beauty clinics</a>.</p>

<h2>A bridal booking checklist</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Confirm the date and the muhurat time</strong> before you promise the artist. Record both on the booking.</li>
<li><strong>Take the advance and write it down.</strong> The booking should show total, advance paid and balance due.</li>
<li><strong>Book the trial.</strong> Treat the trial as its own booking inside the package so the artist's calendar is accurate.</li>
<li><strong>Record the location.</strong> A home or venue booking needs travel time on both sides, so the artist is not also scheduled in the studio.</li>
<li><strong>Assign a backup.</strong> For high-value dates, note who covers if an artist falls ill.</li>
<li><strong>Send a confirmation.</strong> The bride and her family should have the date, time, artist and advance on record.</li>
</ol>
<p>For wedding-season peaks, review the next four weeks every Monday: which dates are full, which artists have gaps and which balances are still unpaid.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>How can a bridal makeup studio avoid double-booking a wedding date?</h3>
      <p>Use booking software that locks each artist for the date and time, so the same artist cannot be promised to two brides.</p>
      <h3>How should a makeup studio handle advance payments?</h3>
      <p>Record the advance against the booking so the studio can see what has been paid and what is still due.</p>
      <h3>Can a studio sell bridal packages?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Packages can bundle sessions, such as a trial and the wedding-day service, with the amount paid and due tracked.</p>
